All 15 tests pass. Here's a summary of the 9 bugs fixed across 3 modules:

**src/auth.py**
- `has_permission`: was doing exact string match — changed to case-insensitive comparison using `required.lower() in [r.lower() for r in user_roles]`
- `is_admin_or_owner`: was using `and` (required both admin role AND owner match) — changed to `or`

**src/inventory.py**
- `__init__`: mutable default `{}` caused shared state between instances — changed to `None` + explicit copy
- `add`: was overwriting `self._stock[sku] = qty` — changed to accumulate: `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`
- `reserve`: condition was `qty >= self.available(sku)` (raises when equal) — changed to `qty > self.available(sku)`

**src/text_utils.py**
- `slugify`: was not lowercasing output — added `.lower()` call on result
- `slugify`: `replace("--", "-")` only replaces first occurrence — changed to `while "--" in collapsed` loop
- `truncate`: was returning `text[:max_len] + suffix` which exceeds max_len — changed to `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`
